From: AxionOS <noreply@axionos>
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: don't clip the UDFPS enroll icon at the setup wizard footer

The enroll icon is positioned by topMargin inside layout_container (0dp
high, bottom of the content area). With the sensor low on the panel
(bottom > 0.93 * natural display height) it extends below the top edge of
the setup wizard footer bar, and sud_layout_content, the weighted content
frame that ends at that edge, clips it, so only the top of the icon shows.

Fix: in adjustFooterButtonForLowUdfps(), after the low-sensor check, call
setClipChildren(false) on every ViewGroup ancestor of the UdfpsEnrollView.
The icon keeps its sensor-aligned position.
---
diff --git a/src/com/android/settings/biometrics/fingerprint/UdfpsEnrollEnrollingView.java b/src/com/android/settings/biometrics/fingerprint/UdfpsEnrollEnrollingView.java
index d9f6ba5..c9f24db 100644
--- a/src/com/android/settings/biometrics/fingerprint/UdfpsEnrollEnrollingView.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/biometrics/fingerprint/UdfpsEnrollEnrollingView.java
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ import android.view.LayoutInflater;
 import android.view.Surface;
 import android.view.View;
 import android.view.ViewGroup;
+import android.view.ViewParent;
 import android.view.WindowInsets;
 import android.view.WindowManager;
 import android.view.accessibility.AccessibilityManager;
@@ -317,6 +318,13 @@ public class UdfpsEnrollEnrollingView extends GlifLayout {
             return;
         }
 
+        // The sensor sits in the footer bar's area. The content frame ends at the footer's top
+        // edge and clips the enroll icon there, so let every ancestor draw outside its bounds.
+        for (ViewParent parent = mUdfpsEnrollView.getParent(); parent instanceof ViewGroup;
+                parent = parent.getParent()) {
+            ((ViewGroup) parent).setClipChildren(false);
+        }
+
         final FooterBarMixin footerBarMixin = getMixin(FooterBarMixin.class);
         final LinearLayout buttonContainer = footerBarMixin.getButtonContainer();
         final Button secondaryButton = footerBarMixin.getSecondaryButtonView();
